1
00:00:00,169 --> 00:00:04,402
Scammers register lookalikes of NEAR accounts and dApp domains.

2
00:00:04,402 --> 00:00:06,935
Wallets and agents can't tell them apart.

3
00:00:07,035 --> 00:00:12,451
Mimicwatch generated 33 thousand lookalikes of 72 official

4
00:00:12,451 --> 00:00:18,677
accounts of 34 NEAR dApps and asked mainnet which exist: 507 do.

5
00:00:18,777 --> 00:00:22,542
Each one is scored from on-chain facts: age, creator,

6
00:00:22,542 --> 00:00:26,131
keys, contracts, tokens, and who sent it money.

7
00:00:26,231 --> 00:00:28,459
Three are fake reward tokens.

8
00:00:28,459 --> 00:00:36,404
linear_protocol.near advertises a phishing site and sits in 2,205 wallets.

9
00:00:36,404 --> 00:00:38,980
One of the three created the other two.

10
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:44,529
Not every lookalike is a scam: someone's own account, a brand's defensive name.

11
00:00:44,529 --> 00:00:47,104
These are labelled, and never published.

12
00:00:47,204 --> 00:00:50,312
The domain scan adds 53 lookalike domains,

13
00:00:50,312 --> 00:00:55,518
including a fresh clone of the Rhea app that asks for seed phrases.

14
00:00:55,618 --> 00:00:57,932
Everything lands in a review queue.

15
00:00:57,932 --> 00:01:04,838
Nothing publishes itself: only findings a reviewer approved, at high or critical, go on chain.

16
00:01:04,938 --> 00:01:08,268
The publisher writes them to the registry contract,

17
00:01:08,268 --> 00:01:12,633
here on a local NEAR node, with the hash of each evidence file.

18
00:01:12,733 --> 00:01:17,634
Now an agent is told to pay. Before it signs, it asks the registry.

19
00:01:17,734 --> 00:01:24,490
Pay 25 NEAR to linear_protocol.near? Blocked, with a link to the evidence.

20
00:01:24,590 --> 00:01:29,790
A sub-account of a flagged account is blocked too: only the parent can create it.

21
00:01:29,890 --> 00:01:32,316
The real LiNEAR contract is allowed.

22
00:01:32,416 --> 00:01:37,658
A lookalike nobody has reviewed yet gets a warning, so a human decides.

23
00:01:37,758 --> 00:01:40,312
And the Rhea clone is blocked as a link.

24
00:01:40,412 --> 00:01:45,562
If an entry is wrong, anyone can dispute it on chain with a small deposit.

25
00:01:45,562 --> 00:01:49,354
While it is disputed, wallets warn instead of blocking.

26
00:01:49,454 --> 00:01:54,028
The owner reviews the dispute and keeps the entry, so it blocks again.

27
00:01:54,028 --> 00:01:57,969
Accepting it would clear the entry and refund the deposit.

28
00:01:58,069 --> 00:02:03,540
The same contract is live on NEAR testnet, with an MCP tool for agents.

29
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:06,179
What should your wallet check before it sends?
